          <p class="text-m mt-6 indent-4 xl:w-5/8">
            <i>La Escondida</i> is a hidden protagonist of the film who speaks to us
            through the soul of nature. There is literally a hidden port in
            transition on the Oaxaca coast. Where the place was once baptized
            due to the myth of a kidnapped indigenous woman in colonial times,
            today the place is being discovered due to gentrification through
            tourism and forced environmental destruction. With a personal
            approach, through encounters with construction workers and turtle
            conservationists, the film shows the exploitative working conditions
            of the locals.
          </p>
